"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T19:08:18-08:00","id":41456,"title":"","content":"Oh, no! I meant Awakening! I am very sorry for the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T19:23:18-08:00","id":41461,"title":"","content":"Happens to all of us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T19:33:24-08:00","id":41465,"title":"","content":"Since it's Awakening I'd be up for a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T19:40:12-08:00","id":41467,"title":"","content":"I might as well, depending on how it sounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:19:18-08:00","id":41505,"title":"","content":"Time to crack open the Awakening book that I do happen to physically possess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:37:45-08:00","id":41510,"title":"","content":"Yeah I've got to re-read up MtAs. It's been quite some time since I've touched it. Either 2009 or 2010 since I've played it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T06:49:37-08:00","id":41680,"title":"","content":"If this is Awakening and not Ascension, then my mistake. I'll quietly make my exit, as I don't have the rules for Awakening","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:35:20-08:00","id":41783,"title":"","content":"What sort of game do you see this as being, OP? Obviously the sort of people drawn by one of the Bound are going to be fairly ambitious and potentially militant members of the Awakened community - could you give some indication of the possible themes that you'd be dealing with in this? Very interested, by the way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1896-winnersh-3","name":"Winnersh 3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1896_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T20:38:32-08:00","id":42130,"title":"","content":"Camilla, I deeply regret any false hope I created. I can tell that any game would be lucky to have you as a player.<br /> <br /> Winnersh 3, my themes would be risk and reward, I guess. One of the first story point would be a mysterious NPC trying to form a cabal in the aftermath of the Hoax to help her with an epic, dangerous quest. In my head, I see the players among those asked to join, but I have not deluded myself into thinking everyone will neatly join up. One of the great things about play by post games is different characters can wander off on their own without harming anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:02:19-08:00","id":42655,"title":"","content":"I'm also interested, although I'm kind of lost on how this is going to run","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1111-egreham","name":"egreham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:48:15-08:00","id":42673,"title":"","content":"In general, I think this game will work by players reacting to previous events from the POV of their characters or NPCs that they might bring to the table with them. The one thing that I think will be necessary is for everyone (very much including me) to avoid as well as possible is making decisions for other players. More than ever, we will have to work together to create a great story. I will provide a short example of what I mean:<br /> <br /> <br /> Player of Titus writes: Titus finds he has been left alone in the waiting room with Barbara. As long minutes slip away, he looks over to his new companion and wonders exactly what she can do. Before he can strike a conversation, he spots a softball sized spider crawling across under one of the waiting room seats.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Barbara, look at that!&quot; cries Titus in alarm. Not for the first time, he wished that he knew even a bit of life.<br /> <br /> <br /> Player of Barbara writes: At Titus' cry, Barbara spots the over-sized spider. ....<br /> <br /> <br /> The above example is silly and purposely short, but I hope shows something what I mean. All of us will be depending on each other to craft a story. It should be great fun, and I think it will work out better than it might sound like it would now.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Editing error 01-04-2014, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:51:39-08:00","id":43187,"title":"","content":"Oops - sorry for the belated reply. That sounds cool - I've had a few ideas for a potential character who might fit well into that. Most of the ideas I've had so far have been fairly political in nature, but I guess that even in the most mystically-focused tomb-robbing quest, mage-wrangling is always a going concern.<br /> <br /> As someone who's played a few PBP-type games before (not that I'm saying you haven't but this is my experience), my two suggestions would be to avoid splitting the party/group/player base up <i>too </i>much - when I've STed/GMed in the past on a PbP basis, it can create quite a bit of work to keep everyone's little narrative going, let alone synced up - and it's worth using a bit of fiat to encourage the characters to join up. A bit of Fate/Time magic can probably indicate to the interested parties that it'd be a good idea, and I think we can all suspend a little belief in the interests of a decent story! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1896-winnersh-3","name":"Winnersh 3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1896_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:35:24-08:00","id":43207,"title":"","content":"Winnersh 3, your advice is well taken, and only a fool would fail to at least listen to any counsel given. I think the group staying together would be good, but events at times have a life of their own. By the way, I also think there will most definately be a place in the game for a political character or characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T18:27:19-08:00","id":43260,"title":"","content":"I'm interested, if you've still got an opening available. Are you using the stop-gap <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/314-stop-gap-god-machine-mechanics-for-mage\">God-Machine update</a> or the pre-God Machine rules for Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:08:20-08:00","id":43304,"title":"","content":"Welcome, AdamantineRapier! My thought was to use pre-God Machine, if only in view of my own ignorance. Of course, most results will decided by players themselves rather than rolled due to the nature of a play by post game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:45:56-08:00","id":43731,"title":"","content":"Excellent - I'm really looking forward to this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1896-winnersh-3","name":"Winnersh 3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1896_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:09:42-08:00","id":43803,"title":"","content":"As to character creation, I think players should start out with nine Points of Arcana. Characters start with 3 Gnosis, and will also have eighteen points of Merits to distribute as you see fit. Attributes and Skills are not required to be selected, but some players have may to do so. As I said, most things will be decided rather than rolled due to the nature of the game. <br /> <br /> Example format: <br /> Name: of course. Birth name &amp; Shadow Name.<br /> Location: City/Town, Country, and Continent.<br /> Path:<br /> Order:<br /> Virtue and Vice: Virtue &amp; Vice give a quick glance at basic motivations.<br /> Arcana: Shows what sort of magic the character has access to.<br /> Backstory:<br /> Additional Suggestions: Merits: Gives an idea of what sort of resources your character can bring to bear when solving problems. Strongest Attribute: Just name one, no need for dot levels. Gives an idea of how your character is likely to solve problems. Weakest Attribute: Gives an idea of what sort of situations your character might find particularly challenging.<br /> <br /> This is the format used in the epistolary games and I think would work well for a play by post game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T21:26:08-08:00","id":43952,"title":"","content":"Name: Winston Jones<br /> Shadow Name: Oberon<br /> Path: Acanthus<br /> Order: Free Council<br /> Legacy: Threndrodist<br /> Virtue: Hope, Vice: Sloth<br /> Arcana: Time 3, Fate 2, Space 4<br /> Backstory: Born in a fairly happy family, he was a really nerdy guy, who was going to university doing Engineering, when, during a bout of particularly bad sleep deprivation, he Awakened to the Tower of Lunargent Thorn, and while his spirit was in Arcadia, he came across a girl who was fleeing a cruel faery lord who had kidnapped her from the mortal world and twisted her into something inhuman. Taking her by the hand, he fled with her to the Tower, and once he signed his name upon the wall, he pulled her with him as he awoke. Lacking anywhere else to go, she began living with him, and soon they started dating. His introduction to the rest of the supernatural world occured soon afterwards, as he discovered one of his professors was also a Mage, a member of the Free Council. His initiation to that body was soon to follow, followed shortly afterwards by his initiation into a group of scientist-mages known as the Threnrodists.<br /> Merits: Retainer 5 (Changeling Girlfriend), Resources 3, Status (Free Council) 3, Library* (Faeries, Quantum Mechanics, Supernal Spirits) 3 , Sanctum* 3<br /> Strongest Attribute: Intelligence, Weakest Attribute: Manipulation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1878,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","user":"AdamantineRapier","date":". 01-07-2014, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:48:01-08:00","id":44577,"title":"","content":"Character fully written up! Bleargh, just realised that I wrote it way too long as well - hope that's OK.<br /> <br /> She's an Acanthus too, but of a very different stripe to Oberon - a magically adept duellist and regal Th\u00e9arch aristocrat, who shamelessly abuses her skill at Fate to politick and pursue power and standing. Powerful, and by the Throne does she know it.<br /> My last couple characters have tended to be austere outsiders to Order and Consilium society, with serious moral qualms about their gifts, and explored issues of whether or not the Star Ladder is something that should be rebuilt - this character is going to be the opposite, with a refreshingly worldly character who's a paid-up and zealous adherent of the Atlantean orthodoxy. And style! And a (worrying mythically significant) sword! As her Shadow Name suggests she started out kinda based on Eliza Doolittle from My Fair Lady, with the idea of being 'lifted up' from her previous existence, both materially and spiritually, and who simply hasn't stopped climbing - she's politically ambitious, and very much prepared to act on her designs to secure and expand the Silver Ladder's influence. Beyond that, I see her as dealing with issues of life transitions, coming into power, and what remains - how the different lessons she's learned at different stages of her life interact, come into conflict, and clash.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow name</b>: Doolittle<br /> <b>Name</b>: Genevi\u00e8ve Kateb<br /> <b>Concept</b>: My Fair Awakened Lady/right hand of the Th\u00e9archs<br /> <br /> <b>Path</b>: Acanthus<br /> <b>Order</b>: Silver Ladder (rank: Claviger)<br /> <b>Legacy</b>: Sisterhood of the Blessed<br /> <br /> <b>Vice</b>: Lust. <i>The privileges afforded to Doolittle by her station are extensive, and have largely insulated her from the consequences of her actions. This isn't always - or even usually - sexual lust, but she's not one to deliberate much or hold back if her blood's up and something's at stake.</i><br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Justice. <i>She doesn't only pursue power for its own sake (although that's mostly it), but also out of a sense of injustice at the Exarchs, the Seers, the grinding inequity of the Fallen World. Naturally, in her just view of the world, she and the Ladder are at the top of the pyramid, and people have criticised her - somewhat justifiably - as using this as a kind of portable moral high ground as a moment's notice. Nonetheless, she does have a deep-rooted sense of justice and dissatisfaction at the order of the Fallen world, even if it manifests in self-aggrandising ways more often than not.</i><br /> <b>Location</b>: Doolittle originally hails from the Toulouse Consilium (France), although she's fairly peripatetic; her loyalties lie much more with her Order than her place of birth, and so she's travelled quite a bit around Europe and North Africa.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: luxury \u2022\u2022, status (Silver Ladder) \u2022\u2022\u2022, striking looks \u2022\u2022, linguistics \u2022\u2022 (English, Atlantean (Secrets of the Ruined Temple p127), library (Atlantean sociology) \u2022, imbued/enhanced item (Durandal) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022 (Banishers p69). Free: High Speech.<br /> <br /> <i>Doolittle is what she is; one of the right hands of the Vox Draconis, a precocious, travelling Claviger of the Ladder ready to represent their interests and make sure the Th\u00e9archs get their representation in any Pentacle conflict or conclave. She's not independently wealthy - her financial backing comes from her Order, dress-maker's bills and plane tickets charged to the Ladder's accounts as a necessary operating cost of good Awakened diplomacy. To underline her status and the authority she represents, she's been given a basic training in Atlantean culture and the surviving rudiments of its language; her knowledge of English, while theoretically fluent, always seems to rapidly desert her whenever she gets into a tiresome conversation with an Anglo. The sword on her hip is a new, somewhat incongruous addition to her ensemble, that raised eyebrows when she appeared at Consilium with it, but Durendal's status as a historical symbol of power, majesty, and conquest is fairly meaningful to anyone who knows its history.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Arcana</b>: Fate 5, Mind 2, Time 1 (assuming the fifth arcana dot costs two dots - if not, Fate 5, Mind 2, Time 2).<br /> <br /> <i>Doolittle makes little pretense at being a widely-read mage, instead focusing her studies entirely on the careful cultivation of destiny and the art of serenditious mastery of her world. Mind adepts aren't entirely trusted at diplomatic functions, and besides, First Degree Mastery of the Arcana gives her more votes in Consilium elections.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Strongest attribute</b>: manipulation. <i>If Doolittle had won her current position and status solely on the ground of her privileged upbringing, she wouldn't be able to live with herself. Instead, it's only mostly because of her upbringing; she's canny enough to be able to take advantage of a good thing, and surf the existing currents of fate, society, interaction so that things always come up Doolittle.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Weakest attribute</b>: resolve. <i>For all that Doolittle may be unflappable and composed, she's a little flighty in the longer term; her post-Awakening life hasn't really persuaded her of the virtue of long-term dedication and steely resolve, especially since she can use her supernal will to shift the odds a little. It'll all turn out right in the end, anyway.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Backstory: </b>Rural France isn't a very nice place if you don't fit in. Genevi\u00e8ve Kateb learned that early on; a young mixed-race girl, living in poverty in Rocamadour, a little village in the south of France, she certainly didn't look like, didn't live like the others in her town. She lived alone with her dad, who was nice to her, but so seldom there - always working, sometimes not coming back at night, never there when she really needed him. She dabbled in a bit of petty crime to get by, but, ultimately, resigned herself to the fact that this place just wasn't for her. Petit-bourgeois insularity and anti-maghrebin slurs muttered behind her back would make sure she never escaped the largely hand-to-mouth existence she'd lived in for the first eighteen years of her life, would never even get the cash to move out. What was the point? It'd never change.<br /> <br /> The point. While picking faintly wizened blackberries from scrubby roadside brambles, she pricked her finger on the point of a thorn, and it was that little moment of pain - of shock and drawn blood - that changed her life. A whirlwind Arcadian mystery play - full of rich, tantalising meaning and treasures <i>just </i>incomprehensible to her illiterate and untutored senses - commenced, and before she knew it, she had scrawled her name in mingled blood and pulped blackberries on the grimy porcelain of the bathroom sink.<br /> <br /> As she Awoke, she was observed. She wasn't what the Ladder had been looking for, exactly, but she had awakened on their watch, and they were hardly going to pass up on the chance to sink their claws into a fresh apprentice. And so, a few weeks after she Awoke, she was taken in by her new tutor, the local Silver Ladder Councillor, Karolus Magnus - her father accepted the excuse that she was going to do maid work with depressing ease. Karolus was old money, scion of a long line of Proximi, and he liked the idea of sponsoring a young mage, tutoring her and building her up from nothing as a symbol of his own power. If he could make an examplar of the Silver Ladder's ideals of humanity's supernal perfectibility, then wouldn't that be a powerful example of his political status and skill?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately (or perhaps not), things have got just a little out of hand of late in the Toulouse Awakened community. The young woman was only meant to be an experiment in human and societal malleability; a pet project of the local Th\u00e9arch Councillor of a minor French Consilium to see how much difference old money and elocution lessons could make on someone who, at least until very recently, was very much not the ideal that the Ladder had expected of Sleepers. It seems that Doolittle learned her lessons well; perhaps too well. Between her grasp of Fate magic, her lessons in comportment and conducting herself, and her own raw talent and ambition, she's managed to manoeuver her way up the hierarchy of her Order, smoothing over political controversies, delighting visiting senior Th\u00e9archs, and keeping tabs on the other orders. Before anyone realised what was going on, she'd risen high in the Order, buoyed up on a wave of fortuitous coincidences that she'd always been best-placed to take advantage of, with everyone owing her favours.<br /> <br /> But a Claviger's position - working as herald of the Order - didn't seem to have been enough for her. What good are favours owed if they're not cashed in? What good is power accumulated that moth and rust can destroy - that isn't used to better the world under enlightened leadership? And so, having been lifted up from obscurity once, she's seeking to do so again - but this time under her own power, acquiring the trappings and symbols of authority and slowly entrenching her political position. She's been travelling Europe for some time now, acquiring lore, power, artefacts, and simple political goodwill. One of her greatest prizes (and, indeed, the only one she hasn't passed on to her Th\u00e9arch superiors) has been Durendal, the sword of Roland, prised from the hands of a nest of Banishers down in Ari\u00e9ge. The sword - at least according to legend - was wielded by one of the most famous knights and enforcers of Charlemagne, and was instrumental in the creation of France as a nation state (and, ironically, was used to kill many hundreds of north Africans and Saracens). For her to wield a nation-building sword is a fairly meaningful statement, but it's not purely symbolic either - the weapon's thaumium edge is razor sharp, and more than one Seer and political rival has learned that training in courtly etiquette includes a training in duelling.<br /> <br /> The reason for her presence in Texas isn't entirely clear (a problem complicated by the fact that she tends not to tie herself to long-term plans in the first place). In reality, she travelled to Texas with the vague aim of simply throwing down against one of the Bound; slaying or imprisoning one of the legendary monstrous foes of Atlantis would be a significant feather in her own cap and that of her order. She's tried to disavow any interest in this quest since it was revealed to a be a hoax, and has recast herself instead as simply being there to offer the skills of the Old World Silver Ladder in serving, organising and wrangling the other Awakened. If she ends up earning a raftload of favours and intelligence from the Yanks in the process - that'd be fine ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1896-winnersh-3","user":"Winnersh 3","date":".  Swapping arcana around - Mind 3, Time 1 to Mind 2, Time 2 01-09-2014, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1896-winnersh-3","name":"Winnersh 3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1896_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T03:02:20-08:00","id":44787,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Lar/ Guillermo Eduardo Muniz<br /> <b>Location:</b> Colorado Springs , Colorado<br /> <b>Path: </b>Thyrsus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Guardians of the Veil<br /> <b>Virtue</b> : Temperance<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Wrath <i>Although it is quite hard to anger him when does lose his temper it is comparable to an Uratha's death rage in its blind fury</i><br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Language\u2022( First Tongue), Status\u2022\u2022(Guardians of the Veil), Familiar\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022(Pistol Spirit), Spirit Status\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Master Exorcist\u2022\u2022, Resources\u2022\u2022,FS: Combat Marksmen \u2022(Shoot First) ,FS: Combat Marksmen\u2022\u2022(Tactical Reload)<br /> <br /> <b>Strongest Attribute</b>: Composure<i> From his childhood he learned that it is better it is to control your violent outburst.Unbridled rage clouds judgment and usually makes a situation worse.</i><br /> <b>Weakest Attribute:</b> Presence<br /> <br /> <b>Backstory:</b> Guillermo always had strong connection to the spirit for some inexplicable reason. He could sense the presence of spirits roaming the world around round him sleeping in the objects he encountered. He rationalized this away that man sheathed in shadows was just a normal person wearing a lot of black clothing.That giant hognosed snake was a normal sized snake it just looked bigger due to a skewed perspective. That demon with sliver skin and gold eyes that phased right through the wall and over my bed was just a nightmare. Were all lies he told himself rather than confronting the truth. The connection Guillermo had with the spirit went both ways. Spirit were fascinated for him for reason the couldn't explain lucky for him it was mere an incredibly brief curiosity.<br /> <br /> Well for most spirits anyways unfortunately for Guillermo this curiosity turned into an obsession for a love spirit. Intent to make Guillermo her lover she abducted him spiriting him away to the shadow. When she arrived in the shadow with her conquest another love spirit ambushed her. In the confusion Guillermo escaped and that when his soul ascended to the primal wilds. When he returned to the fallen world he found himself scribbling his name with a witches brews of blood , urine, feces and tears on a rocky outcropping of a sleeping hill spirit. Shortly after he was found by members of the Guardians of the Veil who had been keeping a watchful eye on him due to his strong spiritual connection.Unsurprisingly he proved himself a gifted wielder of spirit magic .Lar uses his talent to guard the veil between spirit and flesh stopping men and spirit alike form abusing each other.<br /> <br /> He has come to Paris Texas because he received a vision from a lesser god of fate not long before the rumor of the bound. The vision shown to him was a possible future where a wound would engulf in the shadow of Paris then spread all the way to the shadow of Dallas. From this scar would bleed foul spirits and demon that would wreak havoc upon the fallen world. When Lar heard news of the bound in Texas he feared the vision might come to pass. Despite finding out about the hoax he has remained because of what he has seen on both sides of the gauntlet. The spiritual landscape isn't the hellhole he had expected quit the opposite it perfect too perfect. Someone is hiding something and Lar needs to know what .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1544-vectorfox","name":"VectorFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1544_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:02:39-08:00","id":45037,"title":"","content":"If there's still room, I'm interested as well. I doubt that there is--and that's great!--but I've had Awakening forever but never got to do anything with it.<br /> Given the tremendous interest people have already voiced, I doubt there's room here. But on the other hand, if there is I'd like the chance to crack open my Awakening book and actually use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T15:36:10-08:00","id":45182,"title":"","content":"I love the characters so far. Mockery, I'd be thrilled if you joined in.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T12:10:46-08:00","id":45756,"title":"","content":"Birth name: Brian Yates<br /> Shadow Name: Winchester<br /> Location: Dallas, TX<br /> Path: Mastigos<br /> Order: Mysterium<br /> Virtue: Courage<br /> Vice: Pride<br /> Arcana: Mind 4, Space 4, Prime 1<br /> Merits:<i> (Will be filled in later, honest! Writing this up at work.)</i><br /> <br /> Strongest Attribute: Resolve -- Fittingly for one of the Mastigos, Winchester has a remarkably resilient mind, and a quiet fortitude that seems too polite to be called stubbornness.<br /> <br /> Weakest Attribute: Manipulation -- On the other hand, he doesn't live up to the stereotype of the subtle Warlock. He can be convincing just fine, but Winchester wears his heart on his sleeve; you'll know full well exactly what he wants.<br /> <br /> <br /> Backstory: <br /> <br /> <br /> Brian is interning at an architectural firm in Dallas. He hadn't intended to end up there, but now that he had a degree he had put out feelers at dozens of firms looking for somewhere he could work and learn in preparation for his license.<br /> <br /> Really, though, it wasn't being accepted at the firm that had made him decide to stay. It was the night before...<br /> <br /> ***************<br /> <br /> With a blank sketchpad in one hand and a rum and coke from the mini-bar in his room, and regarded the clustered skyline of &quot;Big D&quot; from his window. He could see in his mind's eye where there was a gap in the skyline, and pondered what he would place there, if he could...<br /> <br /> Unbidden, he set his pen to paper.<br /> <br /> A tower began to take shape against a rough outline of the city. As he proceeded, Brian reflected that perhaps the skyscraper taking shape was taller than it needed to be. But it wouldn't be right if it were any shorter. And perhaps it loomed ominously, but anything less would be just as wrong.<br /> <br /> He wasn't quite sure when he stopped sketching, and started putting it together in a featureless field, brick by brick, leading a team of wicked-countenanced things in hard hats and smoke-belching parodies of construction equipment in their duty. They tried to deviate from the plan, or laze about, but that wasn't allowed.<br /> <br /> And he wasn't quite sure when he stopped building, only that he turned around, and a faceless man shook his hand, and with giant pair of shears cut a colorless ribbon before the gateway to thunderous applause from the masses. They started to file in, and Brian would have followed them, but the faceless man shook his head--without words, he told the young architect that it wasn't quite time yet. The faceless man pointed to the dedication plaque, and the blank spot on it where the tower's architect engraved his name.<br /> <br /> When he came to--was it really only the next morning?--he couldn't find his sketch anywhere. But that was just as well--he only half-remembered it in his head, and from what he remembered it looked like something out of that big fantasy movie that had come out a couple months ago.<br /> <br /> It was in his portfolio, instead.<br /> <br /> The color drained from his face when it slipped out during the interview, but the firm partner who picked it up looked at it, and then to Brian, and then simply smiled. Nobody else seemed to notice, but their questions and observations stopped soon after, leaving only Brian and the older man. &quot;Do you have any questions?&quot; He asked, his eyes glimmering with amusement and his voice ambiguous as to whether he spoke about the firm or the alien skyscraper Brian had drawn the night before.<br /> <br /> *******************<br /> <br /> Brian Yates had an internship in the firm by the end of the day. He had a place in the Mysterium by the end of the week.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why is he in Paris? Because he's local-ish. Because there's static on the brainwaves of the city saying something is about to go down nearby, even if nobody knows what it is. Because something is tremoring invisibly a couple hours to the northeast, and as much as it pains him to set aside his pet project for a bit, curiosity is getting the better of him, and his ego won't let him sit this one out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T12:42:33-08:00","id":45781,"title":"","content":"I started the game. In the opening, I had Tuesday try to recruit Cire, but fail. This was to show what she wants. Please feel free to relate Tuesday's efforts to recruit your assorted characters and anything else you might want to cover. Have fun, and thanks for giving me this chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Info update 01-09-2014, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T12:46:04-08:00","id":46431,"title":"","content":"Are you accepting anyone more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1111-egreham","name":"egreham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T13:34:12-08:00","id":46463,"title":"","content":"Yes. I look forward to you joining the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T20:21:29-08:00","id":52106,"title":"","content":"Is there still any room? I'd love to play. I've only played a few sessions of WoD games that seem to disintigrate after three sessions. I've got the Awakening book, World of Darkness, and The Tome of the Watchtowers.<br /> <br /> I'm not above begging. Pitifully, if the situation calls for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2029-esuna","name":"Esuna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2029_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T20:22:59-08:00","id":52108,"title":"","content":"Please feel free to join in. We would be glad to have you! The game has already started on the play by post page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T20:26:59-08:00","id":52109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/41221-recruitment-mage-the-awakening-after-the-2003-hoax?p=52108#post52108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please feel free to join in. We would be glad to have you! The game has already started on the play by post page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright! ^_^ I'll come up with a character as soon as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2029-esuna","name":"Esuna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2029_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}